      <h2>Walter Dawes</h2>
      <p>
        With over 28 years of experience as a professional massage therapist, I
        bring a deeply refined, results-driven approach to bodywork. My practice
        integrates advanced techniques including myofascial release,
        craniosacral therapy, and neuromuscular therapy—allowing me to address
        pain, dysfunction, and tension at their root, not just the surface.
      </p>
      <p>
        Throughout my career, I've worked with a wide range of clients, helping
        them recover from injury, improve mobility, and reconnect with their
        bodies. My work is grounded in both clinical precision and intuitive
        understanding, creating sessions that are both effective and deeply
        restorative.
      </p>
      <p>
        My commitment to discipline and performance extends beyond the treatment
        room. I've completed a cross-country fixed gear ride, undertaken a
        24-hour velodrome endurance challenge, and logged thousands of miles in
        training and racing. These experiences give me a unique perspective on
        the demands placed on the body—whether you're an athlete pushing limits
        or someone simply seeking relief and balance.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every session is tailored to your specific needs, with the goal of
        helping you move better, feel better, and perform at your highest level.
      </p>
